//
// AN INTERFACE MEMBER WITH A BODY IS REFUSED (`@FR-G-Iface`, crossed with `@FR-G-Scope`).  "the
// interface has NO bodies", and DEFAULT method bodies are out of scope by design.  The refusal
// today is the parser's generic "Syntax error: unexpected '}'" — it names neither the rule nor
// the cure, so the claim pins only the word every wording of it will keep.
//
// @falsified-at: none — pins a refusal the compiler already makes; the negation cell of a
//   rule that holds, not a fix, so no earlier build is a control for it.
// CHANNEL: expect — the diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: a build accepting a default body compiles the file and leaves the claim unanswered.
// HOLDS: the diagnostic is the same on both backends.

// @EXPECT_ERROR: Syntax error
interface Sz { fn size(self: Self) -> integer { 1 } }

fn main() { }
